msgid "Thermal Guard"
msgstr ""

msgid "Monitors the temperature of the main processor and the modem. If the device gets too hot, it intervenes in up to three protection stages. Stages stay active until you clear them on the status page."
msgstr ""

msgid "General"
msgstr ""

msgid "Thresholds"
msgstr ""

msgid "Temperatures at which each protection stage starts. What actually happens at stage 2 and 3 is set on the Actions tab."
msgstr ""

msgid "Fan"
msgstr ""

msgid "Modem"
msgstr ""

msgid "Actions"
msgstr ""

msgid "What happens when a stage starts. Stage 1 of 3 warns and, if this service drives the fan (Fan tab), sets it to full speed. That cannot be changed."
msgstr ""

msgid "Enabled"
msgstr ""

msgid "Switching this off pauses the temperature checks. Protection stages that are already active stay applied and the fan is not handed back, so a broken fan cannot be hidden by a checkbox. Use Clear on the status page for that."
msgstr ""

msgid "Interval"
msgstr ""

msgid "Seconds between two temperature readings. Values below five seconds are treated as five."
msgstr ""

msgid "Processor temperature source"
msgstr ""

msgid "System file the processor temperature is read from. The default fits most devices; change it only if your device reports its temperature elsewhere."
msgstr ""

msgid "Processor warning (stage 1 of 3)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Stage 1 of 3 starts when either temperature reaches its warning level: a warning, and full fan speed if this service drives the fan."
msgstr ""

msgid "Processor critical"
msgstr ""

msgid "Processor critical (stage 2 of 3)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Processor warning"
msgstr ""

msgid "Processor emergency"
msgstr ""

msgid "Processor emergency (stage 3 of 3)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Modem warning (stage 1 of 3)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Modem critical"
msgstr ""

msgid "Modem critical (stage 2 of 3)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Modem warning"
msgstr ""

msgid "Hold time"
msgstr ""

msgid "Minutes a stage has to last before the next one starts on time alone: stage 2 of 3 if the temperature has not dropped, stage 3 of 3 if it is still rising."
msgstr ""

msgid "Hysteresis"
msgstr ""

msgid "How many degrees the temperature has to fall below the warning level before the device counts as cooled down."
msgstr ""

msgid "Fan control method"
msgstr ""

msgid "Leave the fan to the regulator the device already has, unless it has none. Automatic uses the kernel fan control when the device offers it and otherwise leaves the fan alone. It never picks direct control, which needs the fan's polarity."
msgstr ""

msgid "Automatic"
msgstr ""

msgid "Kernel fan control"
msgstr ""

msgid "Direct fan control (PWM)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Leave the fan alone"
msgstr ""

msgid "Fan identifier"
msgstr ""

msgid "Name the kernel uses for the fan. Change it only if the fan is not found automatically."
msgstr ""

msgid "Control mode to restore"
msgstr ""

msgid "Control mode handed back to the kernel when the stages are cleared and no earlier control mode was recorded. The default fits almost every device."
msgstr ""

msgid "Fan speed file"
msgstr ""

msgid "Only needed for direct fan control."
msgstr ""

msgid "Fan control file"
msgstr ""

msgid "Only needed for direct fan control. Switches the fan chip to manual control."
msgstr ""

msgid "Value for full speed"
msgstr ""

msgid "Required for direct fan control. The raw value that makes this fan spin fastest. Some boards wire the signal inverted, where 1 is full speed and 255 stops the fan. Without this value and the slowest one, the fan is left alone."
msgstr ""

msgid "Value for the slowest setting"
msgstr ""

msgid "Required for direct fan control. The opposite end of the same scale. Together with full speed it states the polarity, and it shows the fan speed as a percentage. Never written to the hardware."
msgstr ""

msgid "Modem temperature source"
msgstr ""

msgid "Automatic tries the known modem commands in turn. Select your manufacturer if detection fails."
msgstr ""

msgid "Quectel (AT+QTEMP)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Fibocom (AT+GTSENRDTEMP)"
msgstr ""

msgid "File"
msgstr ""

msgid "Command"
msgstr ""

msgid "No modem"
msgstr ""

msgid "Modem control port"
msgstr ""

msgid "Serial port the commands are sent to. Automatic checks the usual ports."
msgstr ""

msgid "Lock file for modem access"
msgstr ""

msgid "Prevents this service and other programs from sending commands to the modem at the same time. Point those programs at the same file."
msgstr ""

msgid "Temperature file"
msgstr ""

msgid "Own temperature source"
msgstr ""

msgid "Reads /etc/thermal-guard/hooks/modem-temp, which has to print the temperature in degrees as a whole number. Place the file over SSH; it runs as root and is deliberately not editable from here."
msgstr ""

